---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import refs from '../data/references.json';
import questions from '../data/questions.json';
---
<Layout title="References & acknowledgments — Singlet" active="references"><header class="page-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Sources, connections & acknowledgments</div><h1>References and related work</h1><p>Many ideas are not necessarily invented as much as they are found and remixed.</p></header><div class="references-layout"><aside><p>This bibliography is a map of intellectual connections. It reaches across physics, mathematics, algorithms, complexity, and cryptography.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}references.bib`} download>Download BibTeX <span>↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#acknowledgments">About this work <span>↘</span></a></aside><ol class="reference-list">{refs.map((r,i)=><li id={r.key}><span class="reference-number">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><span class="eyebrow">{r.year}</span><h2><a href={r.url}>{r.title} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h2><p class="reference-authors">{r.authors.replaceAll(';',',')}</p><p class="reference-relevance">{r.relevance}</p>{questions.some(q=>q.references.includes(r.key))&&<div class="reference-questions"><span>Questions</span>{questions.filter(q=>q.references.includes(r.key)).map(q=><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}questions/${q.id.toLowerCase()}/`}>{q.id}</a>)}</div>}</div></li>)}</ol></div><section class="essay-section essay-continuation" id="acknowledgments"><div class="prose"><h2>About this work</h2><p>These ideas were refined through many conversations with researchers across quantum information.</p><p>This framing and the motivating questions were developed from Kunal Marwaha’s notes, voice and text conversations, with AI assistance for editorial synthesis, mathematical illustrations, implementation, and source discovery.</p><p>Attribution feels strange in this new world. Knowledge can come from anywhere, and ideas are often rediscovered and remixed across fields. I hope this project sparks discussion and new ideas that contribute to a shared understanding of quantum computation.</p><p>Corrections are welcome.</p><h3>Continuing the conversation</h3><p>For a correction, an earlier connection, or a question you would like to develop, <a href="mailto:marwahaha@berkeley.edu?subject=Singlet%20research%20perspective">write to Kunal</a> or <a href="https://github.com/marwahaha/singlet/issues">open an issue on GitHub</a>. Please include a question number or a reference when relevant.</p><p>The earlier <a href="https://marwahaha.github.io/quantum-maxcut-reference/">Quantum Max-Cut reference</a> is another entry into this landscape. The present essay follows some of those connections through subsystem spin.</p></div></section></Layout>
